The trailer loop split each trailer into key / whitespace / value, tested ONLY
$val against brand_re, and reassembled ${key}${ws}${val}. The scrub removed the
half that IMPLIES a vendor -- a hostname in the value -- and preserved the half
that NAMES one:

    ^^^^^^ untouched               ^^^^^^ replaced with an absurd phrase

Exactly one distinct trailer key in the whole history matches brand_re, on 13
commits. It was ACCRUING, not historical: the harness appends that trailer to
every agent commit, and two more landed during the read-only session that first
measured it at 11.

OWNER RULING. A branded key becomes `Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad:` AND forces the
value through the rewriter even when the value carries no brand of its own. A
vendor-named key means the whole trailer is vendor provenance, and a scrubbed
key over an intact value would still publish the session id it points at. Three
git-semantic keys are never renamed -- interpret-trailers, %(trailers:key=...)
and DCO validation all key off the exact token.

SECOND CHANGE: the body sweep is bounded to the first and last 10 body lines. A
body hit DELETES THE WHOLE LINE with no marker, and the pattern list contains
ordinary English words. Not hypothetical: `falcon` is a web framework this
project SUPPORTS (it ships falcon.yaml, listed beside django/flask/fastapi), so
an ordinary commit lost both halves --

    BEFORE  feat(routes): detect falcon resource classes
            The falcon analyzer now maps add_route() to its responder methods.
    AFTER   feat(routes): detect a meerkat djing in a Bronto-burger grill shack
                          with a panel of dogs resource classes
            [body line silently deleted]

Vendor self-attribution clusters at the subject and the trailers, and BOTH are
still scanned unconditionally by their own passes. The window narrows only the
body sweep, trading coverage in the middle of a long body for precision. The
owner chose this over the redaction-marker alternative, so a deletion inside the
window is still silent.

VERIFIED BY EXECUTING THE SHIPPED HOOK, not by reading it: branded key + branded
value both replaced; branded key + CLEAN value both replaced; Signed-off-by
verbatim; capitalised Co-Authored-By keeps its key (the nocasematch case, since
this history carries both spellings); idempotent across three passes; no brand
pattern collides with the replacement key; the window spares the middle and
deletes both ends, with a wide-window control that deletes all three as the
non-vacuity floor.

Two fixture bugs found on the way, both mine: the first drafts omitted
Signed-off-by, so they exercised the DCO guard rather than the scrub and read as
a crash; and a window of 1 scanned only the blank separator at body index 0,
because the window counts body lines as they are, blanks included.

